==Spanish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|es|huego}} {{qualifier|rare, mostly obsolete}}
* {{l|es|fogo}} {{q|rare, obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|osp|fuego}}, from {{inh|es|LL.|focus||fire}}, from {{inh|es|la|focus||hearth}}. The form {{m|es|huego}}, which began to be used around 1500, was mostly replaced by the form starting with -f-<ref>https://www.scribd.com/doc/157209215/Diccionario-Critico-Etimologico-castellano-C-F-Corominas-Joan-pdf</ref>. Compare {{cog|pt|fogo}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|fuel}}. Compare also {{cog|en|focus}}. {{doublet|es|foco}}, which is a borrowing from Latin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{es-IPA}}
* {{a|non-standard}} {{IPA|[ˈɸweɣo]|[ˈhweɣo]|lang=es}}
* {{hyph|fue|go|lang=es}}

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m}}

# [[fire]]

===Interjection===
{{head|es|interjection|head=¡fuego!}}

# [[fire]]! {{gloss|cry of distress indicating that something is on fire}}
#: {{ux|es|'''¡Fuego!''' ¡Llame a los bomberos!|Fire! Call the fire brigade/department!|inline=1}}
# {{lb|es|militar}} [[fire]]! {{gloss|cry to order soldiers to start shooting}}

